    "title": "Gulf Shores man falls short, places second on Survivor 50 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kathryn Bruch ,\n1 hours ago\nORANGE BEACH, Ala. ( WKRG ) — A man from Gulf Shores has left the Mamanuca Islands of Fiji without the title of Survivor 50.\nAlabama Primary Election Results 2026 (key race updates) Jonathan Young, 29, placed second behind winner Aubry Bracco in tonight’s season finale of Survivor.\nLOS ANGELES – MAY 20: Jonathan Young attends the Survivor 50 Live Finale at the Paramount Studios lot in Los Angeles, California on May 20, 2026. (Photo by Robert Voets/CBS via Getty Images) Though he fell short, this marks the second time Young has made it to the finale in Survivor after previously placing fourth during Season 42.\nSupporters at the watch party at The Wharf say representing the Gulf Coast on a national stage is already a huge accomplishment.\nSupporters watched the season finale of Survivor 50 at The Wharf in Orange Beach. (Photo by WKRG News 5’s Kathryn Bruch) While the crowd was hoping for a hometown victory, supporters say they’re still proud of Young’s run this season.\n“I feel like I finished in such a way that I’m proud of,” Young said following the loss. “Not just that, but I heard the third time’s the charm.”\nMobile County Sheriff Paul Burch, incumbent, wins Republican nomination in Alabama Primary Election Young watched the results unfold in Los Angeles during the live broadcast.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "ORANGE BEACH, Ala. ( WKRG ) — A man from Gulf Shores has left the Mamanuca Islands of Fiji without the title of Survivor 50. Alabama Primary Election Results 2026 (key race updates) Jonathan Young, 29, placed second behind winner Aubry Bracco in tonight’s season finale of Survivor. (Photo by Robert Voets/CBS via Getty Images) Though he fell short, this marks the second time Young has made it to the finale in Survivor after previously placing fourth during Season 42.",
